# Copy to .env and fill in. Not committed (see .gitignore).
#
# Running the backend NATIVELY on the Mac (needs msodbcsql18 via Homebrew):
#   DB_SERVER=localhost,1433
#
# Running the backend in DOCKER (see Dockerfile / README) — from inside a
# container, "localhost" means the container itself, not your Mac, so point
# at the host instead:
#   DB_SERVER=host.docker.internal,1433
DB_SERVER=host.docker.internal,1433
DB_NAME=taxidb
DB_USER=sa
DB_PASSWORD=Taxi2026Pass
DB_DRIVER=ODBC Driver 18 for SQL Server

# NOTE: branch Area (the original's c:\meesql.cfg) is NOT a server-side
# setting here. This backend can serve browsers from multiple branches, so
# each request carries its own `branch_area` field (sent by the frontend,
# which holds a per-workstation value set once — see frontend branch setup).

# NOTE on movein.dat (Hashavshevת export) delivery: no backend config
# needed. Confirmed 2026-09-27 that it's always generated from a browser
# already running ON the accounting PC (GET /api/reset/{resetNr}/movein.dat,
# used by both the past-reset lookup screen and the "העברה לחשבשבת" screen)
# — the browser's own download IS the delivery. Point that browser's
# default download folder at CFG.hdir's real value (e.g. "C:\hmon12")
# instead of the usual Downloads folder. A backend-push file-bridge
# mechanism (MonitexFileBridge.ps1 + MOVEIN_BRIDGE_URL) existed briefly for
# a cross-machine scenario that turned out not to apply, and was removed.
